{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>You shall not take interest from your brother.</b> Since he mentioned the foreign slave, even though it is written about him \"you shall not oppress him,\" you have permission to take interest from him." "<b>You shall not take interest from your brother.</b> There is a difference between תשך and תשיך. The meaning is: do not accept from your brother that he give you interest — he too transgresses the commandment of interest. Now, the word applies to two parties. And many say that תשיך is like תשך, there is no difference between them; and likewise there are many instances of this form in Scripture."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:32.334756107Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}